{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits","id":556933,"title":"Basic - and possibly outdated questions about Incarnas & spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-16T08:50:40-07:00","id":556933,"title":"Basic - and possibly outdated questions about Incarnas & spirits","content":"About Incarnas:<br /> - What is the difference between an Incarna and a Celestine?<br /> <br /> - What is an <b>orphaned</b> Incarna? What difference does condition make in one?<br /> <br /> - Are there Incarnas that are <b>not</b> totem spirits?<br /> <br /> <br /> About spirits in general:<br /> - Can a spirit that has crossed the Gauntlet stay immaterial or <b>must</b> it become physical while in the material realm?<br /> <br /> - Can an immaterial spirit be seen in this state or must one use gifts or other supernatural powers to see them, even though they already crossed?<br /> Or would a spirit require a specific charm to <b>make itself visible</b> while immaterial, if it wished to?<br /> <br /> - Are there spirits <b>without</b> the capacity to materialize?<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry if the questions sound sort of noobish, but it has been more than a decade since i last played Werewolf, so my memory is far from trustworthy in that sector and i don't have the books with me - not to mention i suspect my doubts might relate in part to older editions fluff, so the doubts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> edit: it's quite bothersome that once written, the forums won't let you edit even something as little as a space or sign in the title, even with no answers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-16-2015, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:52:41-07:00","id":557020,"title":"","content":"Celestines are the Incarna of planets, stars, and other large objects that exist in the material worlds. They are more powerful then other Incarna because they have been around for much longer and have become representations of other things.<br /> <br /> An orphaned Incarna has lost its material world counter part, an example would be Mammoth who survives as a member of Griffons brood even though his material counter part has since gone extinct. Spirits like this who no longer have a material counter part begin to fade from the Umbra. Normally they need to take refuge in umbra realms or survive on the essence of stronger spirits.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of Incarna that are not totem spirits, but they often stay out of the affairs of the material world so you don't come in contact with them in most games that don't revolve around the Umbra.<br /> <br /> A spirit does not need to materialize but they do need to have a vessel then. Spirits either material, possess, or mind control to interact in the material world for long periods of time. They can project themselves with charms I believe but they aren't actually crossing the Veil when they choose to do that. There are also gifts thats that allow you to sense with spirits are near. There are spirits that can not do any of these things. They are simply to weak to exist outside of the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T10:05:38-07:00","id":557043,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers, they are helping me considerably with organizing thoughts in how to adapt some old half-baked old book stuff from - let's<br /> just say i'm tinkering with a peculiar brand of spirit, so to speak. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So an orphaned Incarna is one that cuts all ties to the physical realm to survive after its material counterpart ceases to be? Hmmm, doesn't look like i might have expected....<br /> <br /> Would an orphaned incarna have some reason to return to the material world, or believe it could regrow in power there, if not impended by a lack of access?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-16-2015, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T10:18:22-07:00","id":557048,"title":"","content":"They don't really cut ties, its that trying to exist without a material counterpart weakens them greatly and they start to fade out of existence. Other realms that represent the tie period they were from are just better suited for them to remain alive in one way or another. <br /> <br /> It could potentially come back, if it came to represent something those in the material world could gather to. Incarna like Griffon, Pegasus, Unicorn, etc have no material counter parts to themselves yet they continue to thrives because they have found some ideal that can be embraced by those in the material world. The same goes for spirits like Minotaur who were cut off from the material world for a long time but were later rediscovered by those who would trade their loyalty for power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T12:48:59-07:00","id":557225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits?p=557020#post557020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestines are the Incarna of planets, stars, and other large objects that exist in the material worlds. They are more powerful then other Incarna because they have been around for much longer and have become representations of other things.<br /> <br /> An orphaned Incarna has lost its material world counter part, an example would be Mammoth who survives as a member of Griffons brood even though his material counter part has since gone extinct. Spirits like this who no longer have a material counter part begin to fade from the Umbra. Normally they need to take refuge in umbra realms or survive on the essence of stronger spirits.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of Incarna that are not totem spirits, but they often stay out of the affairs of the material world so you don't come in contact with them in most games that don't revolve around the Umbra.<br /> <br /> A spirit does not need to materialize but they do need to have a vessel then. Spirits either material, possess, or mind control to interact in the material world for long periods of time. They can project themselves with charms I believe but they aren't actually crossing the Veil when they choose to do that. There are also gifts thats that allow you to sense with spirits are near. There are spirits that can not do any of these things. They are simply to weak to exist outside of the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestines aren't Incarnae. They are above Incarnae, and just under the Triat. They are the things - concepts or heavenly bodies - to which they are associated. Incarnae are merely representatives of the Celestines, and their like can be made by the relevant Celestine promoting a Jaggling to the station of Incarna.<br /> <br /> Also, Incarnae are much more resilient than you've described. Rorg still threatens to play a game of Asteroids For Keeps to take out as many Wyrmspawn on Earth as possible. And Rorg technically never really got a planet to represent. Yet, still, there is a Celestine there, with Rorg warming up his pitching arm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T19:23:03-07:00","id":557737,"title":"","content":"Most of the questions were covered already. Just touching on the ones that may not have been specifically.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits#post556933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About spirits in general:<br /> - Can a spirit that has crossed the Gauntlet stay immaterial or <b>must</b> it become physical while in the material realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits are never really immaterial. In the Umbra, they are more or less solid (as far as Garou as concerned) unless they have, and use, a charm that says otherwise. The most common way for a Spirit to enter the material world is to use the Charm Materialize, which makes them quite solid, with health levels and everything. Depending on the edition (I believe), Agg damage to them will do both health levels and power points. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits#post556933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Can an immaterial spirit be seen in this state or must one use gifts or other supernatural powers to see them, even though they already crossed?<br /> Or would a spirit require a specific charm to <b>make itself visible</b> while immaterial, if it wished to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Expanding on the answer above: depending on circumstance, it might be hard to notice some spirits. For example: a Water Spirit materialized in a river might be tough (or impossible) to actually spot. Aside from situations like that, some spirits have Charms that make them hidden which would function perfectly fine if they materialized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits#post556933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Are there spirits <b>without</b> the capacity to materialize?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them. Aside from outside assistance (Gifts, Spheres, etc), Spirits need to use the Materialize Charm to cross over. Some Spirits can project through, but the systems for that will be covered under the specific Charm used.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T20:04:28-07:00","id":557759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits?p=557737#post557737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of them. Aside from outside assistance (Gifts, Spheres, etc), Spirits need to use the Materialize Charm to cross over. Some Spirits can project through, but the systems for that will be covered under the specific Charm used.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And practically speaking, even having Materialize is sharply limited in use, since a spirit can't materialize if its Gnosis doesn't at least equal the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T05:52:03-07:00","id":558127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits?p=557759#post557759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And practically speaking, even having Materialize is sharply limited in use, since a spirit can't materialize if its Gnosis doesn't at least equal the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really haven't read much of the material that got brought into W20 as far as spirits but the Appear charm used to allow them to project into the material world without actually materializing. Its more practical and the weaker spirits can use this charm to interact with the material world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:16:52-07:00","id":558395,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, nice, nice, some good bits and food for thought here. Well, let me show a bit of what i'm working with and and let's see what how you help me in tinkering with it.<br /> <br /> Edited out NPC names &amp; such, because weren't really important and might spoil things if one of my players is around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The Intruder - This powerful entity seeks entry onto the physical plane of Earth at any cost. For those who use Werewolf, consider the Intruder an orphaned Incarna who has lost a great deal of power during the many millennia it has been orphaned. Being orphaned has also kept it from reentering this plane, where it could begin to rebuild its power.<br /> <br /> One of its servants has taken possession of a experienced paranormal researcher's body and mind, directing him <b>to create a device both magical and technological</b>, which will act as a door to the Intruder's spirit realm, using as the gate's power source a [corrupt] fetish (of Black Spiral provenance) it stole from a captured ronin garou that accidentally showed the way by breaking into its realm (due to the malicious magical item's influence).</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> So from this quick resume in the books, here are some things i have guessed about the Intruder's nature:<br /> <br /> - Its exile into the Umbra is not merely a choice. In fact its realm is <b>locked out</b> of any interaction with the Gauntlet, if not most other parts of the Umbra too.<br /> <br /> - It has no fear of extinction by physically crossing the Gauntlet, quite the contrary in fact, it cherishes that as an opportunity to recover its former power.<br /> <br /> - While possibly corrupt and potentially harmful to Gaia (main reasons the fetish probably threw the poor ronin into its realm), the entity itself (based on its isolated and weakened condition at least) is <b>not </b>of the Wyrm per se. Alternately, the reason the fetish homed on it might (hypotetically) be some long lost connection, either as an ally/patron or long imprisoned nemesis, of the White Howlers.<br /> <br /> - It is somehow &quot;too big&quot; to simply use the fetish as a shapeshifter or more usual spirit would to cross the gauntlet, needing to content itself with making it the core of a passage it intends to enlarge.<br /> <br /> - Its use of a blend of garou magic with weird science to open the way seems to point out some form of connection to the Weaver (what might also explain its &quot;closed shut&quot; realm), or a paradigm similar to the Technocracy's.<br /> <br /> Later i intend to add some bits on its spirit minions and their qualities (about 2-4 types i would guess), these are my thoughts about the In truder itself so far.<br /> If anyone has questions, criticisms, suggestions or theories of their own to add, it will be very much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:46:54-07:00","id":558945,"title":"","content":"Not so much helpful for this iteration, but if later in your campaign you want to revisit this antagonist, I'd say ruling that there's something to people's paranoid fears about the Large Hadron Collider opening doors Man Was Not Meant To would fit its nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T20:32:23-07:00","id":559020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits?p=558945#post558945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much helpful for this iteration, but if later in your campaign you want to revisit this antagonist, I'd say ruling that there's something to people's paranoid fears about the Large Hadron Collider opening doors Man Was Not Meant To would fit its nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sure is an interesting possibility to tinker with, specially if some of its servants stay on the physical plane after its (hoped for) defeat....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:51:26-07:00","id":559711,"title":"","content":"And now the spirit minions, before i forget myself:<br /> <br /> <i>- <b>Drone</b>: Manifests as a silent bluish vapor, able to animate corpses as zombies or possess vampires (and the use of all their powers, knowledge &amp; speech) by entering them. Capable of impersonating the possessed, but far from perfect. Might be incapable of possessing mortals or other supernaturals, as none of these appear in the adventure.<br /> <br /> - <b>Fleshly Creature</b>: made a composite monstrous body for itself offscreen out of parts taken from several vampires (and possibly ghouls) no other apparent powers. Curiously, this thing precedes the first (afaik) mention of Vohzds in Clanbook: Tzimisce by 1-2 years.<br /> <br /> - <b>Deceiver</b>: visible in immaterial state, capable of assuming other appearances (to pass for the ghosts of a person's loved ones) and mind-reading (to help reinforce the ruse).</i><br /> <br /> The spirit inside the paranormal researcher, that beside the considerable techno-magic know-how (one implied in the adventure itself to go beyond the researcher's actual knowledge) has the capacity to drain the souls of willing or immobilized kindred by touch, may be either a more competent drone or a different spirit altogether. It could go either way depending on ST preference i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:55:54-07:00","id":560305,"title":"","content":"Damn, it has been starting to dawn on me that, with how the adventure's fluff seem to blur the line between spirit realm/realm of dead, combined with some of the minions' peculiarities (ease at possession &amp; poltergeist like effects but almost no materialization, proclivity to interact with corpses/undead) are making me think that the Intruder and its ilk might better fit with the forces of the Underworld or Labyrinth than &quot;normal&quot; Umbra.<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;return to regrow in the world of man&quot; has a bit of a Fallen/Earthbound vibe too, i guess. Got to think how will i play this out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-19-2015, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T04:18:08-07:00","id":560620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits?p=560305#post560305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, it has been starting to damn on me that, with how the adventure's fluff seem to blur the line between spirit realm/realm of dead, combined with some of the minions' peculiarities (ease at possession &amp; poltergeist like effects but almost no materialization, proclivity to interact with corpses/undead) are making me think that the Intruder and its ilk might better fit with the forces of the Underworld or Labyrinth than &quot;normal&quot; Umbra.<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;return to regrow in the world of man&quot; has a bit of a Fallen/Earthbound vibe too, i guess. Got to think how will i play this out...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my games, Demons and Wraiths are just different kinds of spirits. Trying to maintain the crossover rules and maintain balance isn't worth the time it takes when I can just use existing charms or make new ones for missing powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:33:26-07:00","id":560871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits?p=560620#post560620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In my games, Demons and Wraiths are just different kinds of spirits. Trying to maintain the crossover rules and maintain balance isn't worth the time it takes when I can just use existing charms or make new ones for missing powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true. That said my interests were more of style and themes than mechanics per se - the antagonist is supposed to be an &quot;alien being&quot; and i wanted to create a feeling of this, while making it a little more coherent than some haphazardly jumbled together disciplines, so to speak. Crossover rules one may simply ignore or adjust to one's preferences, now crossing over <b>cosmologies</b>, that can be quite annoying, specially when it is one you are already not a fan of, my case with DtF overall.<br /> <br /> But no prob, i already had some ideas to get around the pseudo-biblical claptrap and the translation into garou cosmology is getting helpful and fun, so it wasn't wholly a bad corner after i read some bits here and there to order my thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-19-2015, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:36:31-07:00","id":560975,"title":"","content":"I don't consider it crossing over cosmology. I simply justify it in the existing cosmology. Demon comes from the word Daimon which simply means Spirit. Demons are simply spirits that want nothing to do with the Trait War. Maybe once they were once fallen spirits but they have broken free from Wyrms clutches and now they just choose to advance there own agenda like war mongers during the battle. Most of them want out of the umbra, preferring the world of mortals to the Abyss which is the only other safe haven they have had from Gaia's servants who see them as traitors, Weaver spirits what want to assimilate their power, and the Wyrms minions who want to bring them back to corruption. The Abyss has its own scent though and this how Garou like the Stargazers can tell them from other spirits. (They used to have a gift that allowed them to Sense Demons)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T12:50:17-07:00","id":671209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/556933-basic-and-possibly-outdated-questions-about-incarnas-spirits?p=560975#post560975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't consider it crossing over cosmology. I simply justify it in the existing cosmology. Demon comes from the word Daimon which simply means Spirit. Demons are simply spirits that want nothing to do with the Trait War. Maybe once they were once fallen spirits but they have broken free from Wyrms clutches and now they just choose to advance there own agenda like war mongers during the battle. Most of them want out of the umbra, preferring the world of mortals to the Abyss which is the only other safe haven they have had from Gaia's servants<br /> who see them as traitors, Weaver spirits what want to assimilate their power, and the Wyrms minions who want to bring them back to corruption. The Abyss has its own scent though and this how Garou like the Stargazers can tell them from other spirits. (They used to have a gift that allowed them to Sense Demons)</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, sorry for the long silence - bunch of stuff happened since and i got completely sidetracked from the subject since, only recently returning to it.<br /> <br /> To put it bluntly, my problem at the time of starting the topic was basically in the &quot;justify it in the existing cosmology&quot; sector. While &quot;neutral spirits in the Wyrm War&quot; is simple, that in itself tells me nothing of what character, themes or agenda itself to work into the big bad rogue Incarna and its host of servants. These i mostly got from the adventure i originally found them into, but a number of little details (and the name/title of the boss itself) would bring me to the &quot;fallen angels&quot; connection, one i deeply disliked because i find biblical stuff terribly ill-fitting to WoD's cosmology and portrayal in general. So my hurdle at the time was &quot;ok, how do i use these damn themes/background while kicking the biblical angle out?&quot;<br /> <br /> Then a number of distractions came in the way - including a surgery - i got sidetracked into other things and only this week did i sort of return to the subject, amidst some other Werewolf-related stuff i started to tinker with and truth be told worked out those kinks pretty quickly this time around.<br /> <br /> I basically run with these beings as a host of air spirits in the service of a &quot;Sky Father&quot; figure complementary to the Earth Mother, an Ouranos of sorts. They were the wind/cloud/smoke that turns into lightning/thunder/sparks/fire so to speak and while the original watchers of a race of ape-beings, they intervened with them to an unexpected level, leading those ape-beings, those who might become the next generation of Fera to watch the earth in the next age of the cycle of creation and destruction, the Hanuman, in transforming into something quite different and unpredictable.<br /> <br /> Humanity, <i>inspired </i>by thunder and flame, acutely aware of the ways of <i>transforming things around them</i>, with acts, noise, words, light and flame, twisting their broken potential in directions that would further shape the world instead of <i>changing with it</i> and <i>adapting in harmony</i>. Imbalance upon imbalance that lead to the necessity of the Spirit-Hounds, to manipulate their fist efforts of dominating the animals around them to restrain and maybe guide them toward the path, something that would blow up even harder later on, with Spirit-Hounds deluding themselves into being flesh and their &quot;stagnation&quot; as a Fera race that was never supposed to be, the Garou and debacles like the Impergium, War of Rage and more.<br /> <br /> For this they were punished with imprisonment in far realms of the Deep Umbra. Their inability to cross the Gauntlet on their own and existence in a state at the same time material and ephemeral both owes to both their semi-elemental nature and being sealed in the edges of the Tellurian in a time BEFORE the separation of material &amp; spirit and the Gauntlet's formation. Being unable to<b> cross </b>the Gauntlet as other spirits, they need to <b>burn</b> a way through to enter the world but for this, specially in the case of the resentful Incarna that leads them, it requires something in the world to be consumed in the burning of the road (and hence its contact and manipulation of <i>vampires</i>, that while supernatural are in general quite poor in understanding of the spirit worlds - what doesn't mean they haven't tried - and probably failed - with other supernaturals, leaving potentially useful clues, info and maybe even enemies aware of its threat).<br /> <br /> So that's the gist of things so far and what basis i did set up for an ongoing game. More, probably only after i actually have a chronicle and group actually set up and ready to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-19-2015, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}